v0.7.0 (A16)

- Point the update check and the README install and update links to this fork's releases
- README: name microG 0.3.16 as the first release with the Android Auto flag that Car App Library apps need
- Add an Action button that uninstalls the Android Auto updates after a Volume UP confirmation: on KernelSU-Next, uninstall.sh runs at the next boot before the package manager starts and cannot do it; README Warning and Uninstall point to it
- Stop copying phenotype.db and the Android Auto phenotype .pb file, and drop the phenotype.db overwrite prompt: microG (tested with 0.3.17) does not read phenotype.db, and Android Auto works without the .pb file on the test phone; the installer no longer writes into app data directories, where a planted symlink could redirect the root copies
- Restore IFS at the end of the installer: the value it left behind made Hybrid Mount skip its partition links
- Warn in the installer when the KernelSU metamodule is disabled or marked for removal (metamodules without metainstall.sh; for the others KernelSU-Next refuses the install itself)
- README: state that this fork is maintained mainly for personal use
- Drop Android 11 to 15: the installer stops with an error below Android 16 (API 36), and the Android Auto stub, privapp permissions, overlay and oat files for older releases are removed
- Drop Magisk from the documentation: KernelSU-Next is the only supported root solution (the installer does not block Magisk, but Magisk is not tested)
- Add Android 16 support: newer Android Auto stub, privapp permissions and overlay from NikGapps-Addon-16-AndroidAuto-20260222 (via upstream PR #47 by alpianon); the new privapp permissions also allow Android Auto MANAGE_USERS, MODIFY_PHONE_STATE, POWER_SAVER and TETHER_PRIVILEGED, which the newer stub requests
- Warn in the installer when KernelSU has no metamodule to mount the module files
- Explain in the installer what the stubs are, list the skipped stubs in the summary, and raise the YES/NO prompt timeout from 10-20 s to 30 s
- README: document KernelSU-Next (metamodule, Zygisk provider + Vector, "Umount modules"), the Stubs section, Troubleshooting and Recovery, and the Aurora `Root installer` advice
- README: fix the step 8 list formatting (upstream PR #40 by cnjhb)
- README: rewrite "3rd party apps" from a device test: media apps need only Unknown Sources; navigation and IoT apps need the XLauncher module (Android Auto as only scope) or Aurora's microG install method; root/shell "install as Play Store" methods are no longer recommended for them

